Coverage map: renderer §1 retained geometry and changed-only uploads -> atlas growth, dirty-write, LRU generation/repack, SVG/icon reuse, path retention and 800-draw arena comparison. Public pixels cannot detect unnecessary reuploads, so the explicit upload-efficiency counters remain paired with independent pixel checks. Submission misuse -> both panic checks catch only the violating begin/drop operation, not device setup; recovered begin state flushes before drop. The assertion-free rewind test is removed only because arena_slices_match_per_draw_buffers_across_many_draws_and_mid_frame_growth proves the same next-frame path with fresh-renderer pixels and stable grown capacity.
renderer §1a/§1b/§4.4a native text/blending -> all 16,384 measurement cases, the multilingual glyph-component matrix, alpha/compositing tests, fallback/weight/phase masks, SVG snapping, blur/shadow/rim cap and exact vector tests retained. The rewritten fallback test uses one shared component cache across repeated default, bold and fractional-phase input, comparing dimensions, advance and every mask byte to independently rasterized native lines; it no longer asserts private cache key/font structs. Terminal §4.1/§4.2/§4.3 -> all smoke, fallback/emoji, cursor/decorations, font/size/scale/theme generated pictures retained. rim-glow §7 -> nearest-neighbor text luminance-cap regression retained. No spec acceptance line or invariant check loses a test.

